- A comment can't contain `--` or end with `-`. The check happens when the node is written, and it throws an `XmlException` ("Comments must not contain '--' or end with '-'.").
- `XmlNode.Parse` keeps the comments inside the root element. Comments before and after the root element aren't part of the tree. To keep those through a round trip, use `XmlDocument`, which writes them back in `WriteTo`.
- A comment doesn't contribute to `XmlElementNode.InnerText`.
- `ToString` on a comment returns its markup, such as `<!-- reviewed -->`.
